{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400897-a-profoundly-isolated-society","id":1400897,"title":"A profoundly isolated society","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-03T21:12:46-07:00","id":1400897,"title":"A profoundly isolated society","content":"During the Usurpation, many vehicles were destroyed, or at best wrecked beyond repair, including the submersible passenger-carrying freighter <i>Sarli</i>, lost with all hands somewhere between Wu Jian and the Caul. An enormous vessel, carrying roughly five hundred people, passengers and crew combined, the vessel suffered battle damage that jammed the ballast hatches open, and sent it to the bottom of the ocean. There in the black cold, the vessel settled mostly keel-down on the bottom, and the survivors turned their attentions to the problems of survival. Air and water, provided by air recycling and desalination equipment intended to function indefinitely, were not problems, but food was another matter, for upon the floor of the deep sea, there is no light to nourish crops, and little food filters down so far. By necessity, the people of <i>Sarli </i>have converted their vessel's immense holds into aquaculture tanks, the main draw upon the vessel's power supply being the tanks' sorcerous lamps. The ship draws power from the dragon lines of the sea, its supply inexhaustible but far from limitless; there is enough for some heat, enough that the ship is cool (about 13C/55F) rather that frigid, light for the food tanks, and for the purifiers, but not much beyond, a few lamps in the corridors.<br /> <br /> The battle damage is relatively minor; a single major repair project would be enough to restore the vessel's ability to surface. Unfortunately, the key part needed is too sophisticated to be replaced without Craft(First Age Artifice) and Celestial sorcery, and there were no sorceror-engineers with the needed breadth and depth of knowledge aboard when the vessel sank.<br /> <br /> Obviously, this is the barest outline, but I'd like opinions on it so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 11-29-2020, 12:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T01:26:42-07:00","id":1400912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400897-a-profoundly-isolated-society#post1400897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Obviously, this is the barest outline, but I'd like opinions on it so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it can be assessed without knowing the kinds of stories it is intended to tell.<br /> <br /> It does sound interesting as an opening scenario for a more one-off or one story played out over a few sessions kind of survival and escape chronicle. A kind of undersea The Martian, complete with the need to secure a food source until such time as escape can be devised.<br /> <br /> That would probably require detailing some more of the assets that could be used for escape, even if they are difficult to manage and present high risks unless something creative and difficult is accomplished with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T07:16:03-07:00","id":1400953,"title":"","content":"It is intended as a short-term scenario; the PCs would most likely be either insiders who really, really want to get the <i>Sarli</i> back to the surface, or outsiders who want to recover the vessel (and are not expecting its people). Though once restored, the vessel would be a wonderful base of operations for an island hopping campaign in the West. One thing I've decided is that the tiny population has the highest density of Water Aspects in the world, the descendants of a minor official who was on the vessel to observe its performance, help determine if a <i>Sarli</i> class was warranted. Being the only providers of food outside the tanks, and the only ones who can discourage aggressive sea life, the Water-Children (as they're known) are held in very high regard.<br /> <br /> One thing I have yet to decide is whether or not Creation has an analogue to the bends or to rapture of the depths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 07-04-2020, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T22:49:26-07:00","id":1401064,"title":"","content":"Why wouldn't the water castes have left to get help and come back?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T01:33:49-07:00","id":1401077,"title":"","content":"200 fathoms down and hundreds of leagues from shore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T03:10:59-07:00","id":1401081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400897-a-profoundly-isolated-society?p=1401077#post1401077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">200 fathoms down and hundreds of leagues from shore.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the Water Aspect packs a sandwich or two. They can make it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T07:20:02-07:00","id":1401109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400897-a-profoundly-isolated-society?p=1401077#post1401077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">200 fathoms down and hundreds of leagues from shore.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they can leave the ship, they almost certainly <i>could</i> reach help. You'll want some societal reason that they don't try. If the Sarli went down in the Usurpation, maybe the survivors are convinced that there's no home to go back to and taught their kids that the surface world was destroyed. Or maybe they landed right in the middle of a sea-floor demesne and the immediate environs are incredibly dangerous. OR, a few Water Children <i>have</i> tried to go for help and never returned, so the remaining ones stopped trying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T07:29:38-07:00","id":1401112,"title":"","content":"Alucard: You have no idea how difficult it is to navigate open ocean, do you? I doubt any of the people on the <i>Sarli</i> were skilled in celestial navigation, or Polynesian-style wayfinding, an art that in our world all but died out, and is only now being reconstructed. But even if one of them does reach the shore, it's then necessary to get back, and with a recovery expedition, and who's going to mount it and how? I do not call it impossible; I do call it hard enough to justify the society developing and continuing.<br /> <br /> Blackwell: I agree, there does need to be a societal reason. Currently, I'm working with the idea that the early attempts failed due to societal collapse on the surface (or just inability to find land, or at least land with actual society), and so the people who tried came back empty-handed or not at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 07-05-2020, 10:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T07:39:41-07:00","id":1401115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400897-a-profoundly-isolated-society?p=1400953#post1400953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is intended as a short-term scenario; the PCs would most likely be either insiders who really, really want to get the <i>Sarli</i> back to the surface, or outsiders who want to recover the vessel (and are not expecting its people).</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the idea here that there is a society of people that has been within this ship (how big is it?) for more than a thousand years, and the potential for players in Realm Year 768 to happen upon them? Or is the matter of them being found or resurfacing themselves something that would have happened in the early decades of the Shogunate?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T07:58:00-07:00","id":1401120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400897-a-profoundly-isolated-society?p=1401115#post1401115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is the idea here that there is a society of people that has been within this ship (how big is it?) for more than a thousand years, and the potential for players in Realm Year 768 to happen upon them? Or is the matter of them being found or resurfacing themselves something that would have happened in the early decades of the Shogunate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty darn big. I'm not sure exactly how big, I haven't worked that out yet. My current concept is of outsiders finding the ship in RY 768+ and perhaps raising it. With appropriate complications of course, both physical and social. Currently, I think the people of the<i> Sarli</i> regard the vessel in somewhat the same way as residents of a generation ship: it's their home, but not necessarily their home forever. Naturally, not everyone will favour raising the ship; some will reject the change, others feel threatened. and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T08:32:02-07:00","id":1401124,"title":"","content":"Generation ships are one of those things that I think a person trained in or enamoured of the hard sciences would come up with, before a soft scientist picks it to pieces.<br /> <br /> On a line between realism and deep pulp, where would you want to portray the long term consequences of being in a confined space isolated from sunlight, fresh air and contact with other people?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T08:43:09-07:00","id":1401128,"title":"","content":"More toward the realism end; over the course of their long isolation, the people of the vessel have certainly adapted to their environment by at least having a higher tolerance for cold and pressure, and since the population is so small and the margins of survival quite narrow, well...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T10:56:47-07:00","id":1401149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400897-a-profoundly-isolated-society?p=1401112#post1401112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alucard: You have no idea how difficult it is to navigate open ocean, do you? I doubt any of the people on the <i>Sarli</i> were skilled in celestial navigation, or Polynesian-style wayfinding, an art that in our world all but died out, and is only now being reconstructed. But even if one of them does reach the shore, it's then necessary to get back, and with a recovery expedition, and who's going to mount it and how? I do not call it impossible; I do call it hard enough to justify the society developing and continuing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're grotesquely underselling the Exalted.<br /> <br /> Call it a Difficulty 5 Sail roll to navigate by the stars, and an Int 3 Sail 3 DB with the Sail Excellency is making that on an average roll without a Stunt.<br /> <br /> Who mounts the rescue operation? Literally the Exalted hero who just fought their way to land.<br /> <br /> How do they rescue the others? Aristotle described the diving bell.<br /> <br /> And we're saying there's, what, a dozen of these Exalted champions who could be pulling off this rescue?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400897-a-profoundly-isolated-society?p=1401112#post1401112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blackwell: I agree, there does need to be a societal reason. Currently, I'm working with the idea that the early attempts failed due to societal collapse on the surface (or just inability to find land, or at least land with actual society), and so the people who tried came back empty-handed or not at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean this doesn't not work.<br /> <br /> (The post-Usurpation Creation isn't exactly filled with helpful seafaring engineers.)<br /> <br /> I do, reasonably strongly, feel that an Exalted hero should be able to fight their way to land. And having found land, she probably should at least attempt rescue by herself.<br /> <br /> But it's non-trivial. There's dozens of points of potential failure. Maybe it could even be worked into the story -- an early DB found land, but couldn't find her way back to the ship. Maybe she leaves a diary on an island which us now recovered by the PCs who use it to find the lost ship. Maybe a <i>contemporary</i> DB fights her way to shore and finds the PCs, leading them back to the ship as part of the rescue effort.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> I think it's more elegant just to nix having an enormous population of seafaring demi-gods.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps the Deebs are the problem. Maybe they like it down there and are deliberately holding the humans hostage, directly in opposition to the PCs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-05-2020, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T11:56:50-07:00","id":1401159,"title":"","content":"The population isn\u2019t enormous, only two or three out maybe a hundred total, which is still higher than any other settlement in Creation.<br /> <br /> And I do like the idea of the diary. I\u2019m not entirely sure how I feel about a contemporary DB.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T12:29:02-07:00","id":1401165,"title":"","content":"I wonder if it would make more sense if the local Dragonblooded were <i>not</i> Water aspected? Like, if the officials they descend from were Air, Fire, and/or Wood aspects, which has helped them keep their heat, air, and crops going, but in a great cosmic irony, any Water aspects either perished in the sinking itself (as the only ones who could effectively go out to meet whatever the threat was) or in early rescue attempts.<br /> <br /> Being the only ones able to leave the relative safety of the ship would be a double edged sword, afterall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T12:34:48-07:00","id":1401169,"title":"","content":"Also, there was a society a little like this inthe 2e Underworld book, except it was a whole island that sunk in the Usurpation, and it sunk into the sea <i>and</i> into the Underworld at the same time. It also ended up with a high % Dragon-blooded, because conditions wero so harsh that only DBs lived very long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T20:59:31-07:00","id":1401262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400897-a-profoundly-isolated-society?p=1401128#post1401128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More toward the realism end</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno; that's the end that has to deal with things like inbreeding and the fact of that level of isolation and confinement definitely driving people insane.<br /> <br /> If not actual the actual full-blown hallucinations, dissociation and suicidal tendencies, people in such a situation are liable to become extremely irritable with one another, and there doesn't exactly seem to be much to be occupied with besides sitting around and becoming more and more bothered by the behaviour of others. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">over the course of their long isolation, the people of the vessel have certainly adapted to their environment by at least having a higher tolerance for cold and pressure, and since the population is so small and the margins of survival quite narrow, well...</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of feel as though your focus on things like adaptation to physical factors and the logistics reinforces my point about generation ships being a thing devised by hard scientists that a sociologist or psychologist would bring down in the planning stages. The things you're alluding to at the end there just add to the stresses that people are under.<br /> <br /> Could a society ultimately adapt to such pressures? Possibly, but the proposed starting group is so small that it's hard to believe they wouldn't have wiped themselves out within a generation or two.<br /> <br /> Also the lack of access to sunlight is going to be mentally and physically unhealthy. I'm not sure if that aquaculture will provide them with much vitamin C.<br /> <br /> If nothing else, the scenario in which they're actually discovered by players ought to be the kind of thing that comes with the most extreme kinds of culture shock. Holding out hope for escape for a thousand years... after half that time I'd wonder at the inhabitants even believing that there's anything more to the world besides themselves and the water above.<br /> <br /> By the way, I find the premise that this ocean-going vessel would be crewed by personnel who would not know how to navigate on open water. Even if the ship was fully automated or something, sailing is one of those professions that tends to have a very enduring tradition of planning for the possibility of things going terribly wrong, and that can include being trained in navigational techniques that aren't so dependent on their instruments.<br /> <br /> There's also the matter of how ships tend to log their travel plans before departing port and take consistent and frequently travelled routes for purposes that include the fact that if something goes wrong you're more likely to be happened upon by somebody else that can help. Those kinds of things are why it was ever possible to find sunken vessels decades or centuries after the fact even without survivors popping up to seek help.<br /> <br /> Still, I'm saying this primarily because... well, I think it's interesting, but a close second is to advise not delving too deeply into the can of worms and just softballing the idea. <br /> <br /> Heck, I would suggest just having them happen to land in a deep sea demesne and let the Essence mutate them into a form that could more readily survive in their bubble (although if that also covers for them psychologically then that would just enhance the degree to which I would expect them to come back out strange and alienated)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T22:23:19-07:00","id":1401273,"title":"","content":"As a first age vessel it could have certain fantastical amenities to alleviate those stresses. It\u2019s artificial light may be using sunshard lanterns that burn with real sunlight. I\u2019d be amazed if early on there wasn\u2019t violence, and people going a bit loopy, but once you\u2019ve gotten past the generation where anyone who has been outside the ship before has passed away you might be able to deal with it better.<br /> <br /> If it\u2019s big enough to have a fairly large open space with movable jungle gym style equipment* you could keep active. It would be harder than a colony of people living on an isolated island, but not impossibly harder. They\u2019d have music, art, science, maybe to the point where over the millennia they discovered a kind of fantastical air essence scuba setup that let even mortals or non-water aspected exalted explore the surrounding sea floor. If we\u2019re talking crazy Exalted Earth but even more Extra they might be 20 kilometres deep or more, and with the dragon lines crossing to make a demense to protect them from the crushing depths in a radius around their ship. They might even work out, over god knows how many generations, how to harness that into a proper manse and extend their little bubble further.<br /> <br /> Not to mention at that depth it makes reaching the surface really damn hard for anyone that\u2019s not a very hardy water aspect, although not impossible.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *like if you have at least one room like this<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://images.r.cruisecritic.com/cruiserschoice/2019/Dining_Large_CelebrityEquinox_bestofXs.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://images.r.cruisecritic.com/cr...x_bestofXs.jpg</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T22:27:35-07:00","id":1401275,"title":"","content":"I'd imagine that they'd be on the one side incredibly gregarious, and on the other side, extremely solitary, swinging sharply between the two.<br /> <br /> The lack of sunlight is a potential problem, unless they can synthesize vitamin C, as almost every animal in the world can, and can get vitamin D from their diet. Of course, that assumes that those vitamins even exist in Creation, which is not a given. Indeed, there's evidence that the humours are real, in the form of the Soul-Perfecting Elixir and its accompanying Merits.<br /> <br /> Massive culture shock is pretty much a given and if not the point, then certainly a main point in this scenario.<br /> <br /> I'm a small-craft sailor myself, and I do know a bit about celestial navigation, enough to know that if someone hasn't explicitly trained in doing so, navigating the open ocean without at least charts of some sort is extremely difficult, and if, like a Water Aspect, you don't have the benefit of vessel and crew to keep a mostly-steady course, every time you take a rest, your position changes in an unknown way, so you need to re-establish your position every time you wake up. It's not impossible, I don't claim that, but it's extremely difficult, especially since DB can no longer orient themselves on their elemental poles.<br /> <br /> You're right about logs, but most salvaged vessel are recovered from shallow water, and not after civilization-ending catastrophe.<br /> <br /> Oh, and the <i>Sarli</i> came to rest in what we'd call the mesopelagic zone: very little light, but more than none.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 07-06-2020, 01:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T22:36:24-07:00","id":1401277,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s also this thing about Creation that if you sail east you hit land, if you even knew a little bit if you were north or south you can sail in a particular direction and almost certainly hit the blessed isle even. As long as you can get food at the surface, or take a month\u2019s worth with you it should be doable. Really water aspects are so god damn at home in the water anyway they don\u2019t necessarily need a boat, if they\u2019ve got the survival skills it\u2019s basically a wilderness trek for them. <br /> <br /> That being said, I think the concept is so good that you should just ignore it or if you like come up with some good reasons why that didn\u2019t happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T23:15:32-07:00","id":1401282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400897-a-profoundly-isolated-society?p=1401277#post1401277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There\u2019s also this thing about Creation that if you sail east you hit land, if you even knew a little bit if you were north or south you can sail in a particular direction and almost certainly hit the blessed isle.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. But it's one thing to go from the <i>Sarli</i> to the Blessed Isle, quite another to go from the Blessed Isle to the <i>Sarli, </i>and wilderness treks can still be dangerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T01:46:05-07:00","id":1401297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400897-a-profoundly-isolated-society?p=1401277#post1401277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There\u2019s also this thing about Creation that if you sail east you hit land</div> </div> </div> </div>*looks at the Imperial Mountain*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T09:37:33-07:00","id":1401358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400897-a-profoundly-isolated-society?p=1401169#post1401169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, there was a society a little like this inthe 2e Underworld book, except it was a whole island that sunk in the Usurpation, and it sunk into the sea <i>and</i> into the Underworld at the same time. It also ended up with a high % Dragon-blooded, because conditions wero so harsh that only DBs lived very long.</div> </div> </div> </div>Saigoth being at the bottom of the ocean in the Underworld also helped establish why Water Aspects couldn't simply swim for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T05:30:16-07:00","id":1401465,"title":"","content":"I don't want to get bogged down in what sorcery might imply about biology. Suffice to say that this is the kind of setting that generally acts as though scurvy is a risk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T07:01:50-07:00","id":1401476,"title":"","content":"Bad diet can still unbalance the humours. The problem then becomes one of finding suitable strengthening foods, perhaps some sea-floor plants that thrive wildly in the bright light of the tanks. Back on the topic of society, I think they'd be strongly reactionary, given the difficulty of simply surviving and the risk of any change killing everyone, or at least dropping the population below the threshold of viability. Resources are very scarce, to the point that most people likely wear only loincloths made from tanned fish skins and cord for the central stalks of kelp-analogue water plants, and <i>everything</i> is used and reused to the last, including their dead going to the aquaculture tanks, where they nourish the plants that purify the greywater and allow fish to thrive. The tanks need constant monitoring and the pumps (by now just a series of bladders and valves) are the main drain upon the <i>Sarli's</i> scant resources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T09:22:04-07:00","id":1401921,"title":"","content":"Some research, admittedly minimal due to lack of access to relevant libraries, suggests that <i>Sarli's</i> society would be rather like a monastery's: a heavy emphasis on calm, deliberate action, many customs for easing tensions, strict adherence to a specific ideology and set of customs, austerity as a prime virtue, and due to small size, a lack of actual laws as that term is commonly used. The population is certainly below Dunbar's number, so a judicial or bureaucratic apparatus isn't needed. There will be a Captain and maybe an XO, and that's it; the population's only 60 - 100 people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T21:12:49-07:00","id":1402012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400897-a-profoundly-isolated-society#post1400897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">During the Usurpation, many vehicles were destroyed, or at best wrecked beyond repair, including the submersible passenger-carrying freighter <i>Sarli</i>, lost with all hands somewhere between Wu Jian and the Caul. An enormous vessel, carrying roughly five hundred people, passengers and crew combined, the vessel suffered battle damage that jammed the ballast hatches open, and sent it to the bottom of the ocean. There in the black cold, the vessel settled mostly keel-up on the bottom, and the survivors turned their attentions to the problems of survival. Air and water, provided by air recycling and desalination equipment intended to function indefinitely, were not problems, but food was another matter, for upon the floor of the deep sea, there is no light to nourish crops, and little food filters down so far. By necessity, the people of <i>Sarli </i>have converted their vessel's immense holds into aquaculture tanks, the main draw upon the vessel's power supply being the tanks' sorcerous lamps. The ship draws power from the dragon lines of the sea, its supply inexhaustible but far from limitless; there is enough for some heat, enough that the ship is cool (about 13C/55F) rather that frigid, light for the food tanks, and for the purifiers, but not much beyond, a few lamps in the corridors.<br /> <br /> The battle damage is relatively minor; a single major repair project would be enough to restore the vessel's ability to surface. Unfortunately, the key part needed is too sophisticated to be replaced without Craft(First Age Artifice) and Celestial sorcery, and there were no sorceror-engineers with the needed breadth and depth of knowledge aboard when the vessel sank.<br /> <br /> Obviously, this is the barest outline, but I'd like opinions on it so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>reminds me of an episode of the orville, the one with the gigantic colony ship that was large enough for an entire civilization","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T12:38:31-07:00","id":1402852,"title":"","content":"Question.<br /> <br /> On the problems of sorcery and, well, exalted.<br /> <br /> The deprivation and shit? A bit unlikely. After all, craft charms and such can easily compensate for poorer materials and a lack of tooling (presuming lack of tools in a 1st age ship). And are there any sorcerers? 1? 2? 3? You said that its the highest population of dragonblooded in the world. If there's just one or two, then the problems such as the lack of food and such can easily be solved. Food from the aerial table means that your supplies can be stretched out to near absurdity, in conjunction with the sun lamps.<br /> <br /> You can get water elementals to do shit like go outside and do work. Sorcerous workings can let you do things like 'craft a stone to turn sunlight into grain' or 'create a plant that feeds off ocean currents instead of sunlight'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T13:35:16-07:00","id":1402858,"title":"","content":"Where are these people learning sorcery from?<br /> <br /> (But I agree -- it's much neater with mortals.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T13:54:04-07:00","id":1402864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400897-a-profoundly-isolated-society?p=1402858#post1402858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where are these people learning sorcery from?<br /> <br /> (But I agree -- it's much neater with mortals.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Pardon me, but this is from the first age. It's not unknown for a dragonblooded or two to know sorcery. Even if they don't know sorcery, well, it isn't impossible for someone to awaken sorcery spontaneously from the environment around them. I know its difficult, but this is an environment where something like that is really desired, and hundreds or at least a thousand years to learn it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T22:52:53-07:00","id":1402915,"title":"","content":"The real bar to its residents' repairing the <i>Sarli</i> is the lack of Craft skills, especially Craft(First Age Artifice). Such a small society with such limited resources is unlikely to be able to develop the Lore, Occult and Craft(Artifacts) needed just to underlie the development of the first. Oh, and I said &quot;population density.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T12:20:28-07:00","id":1403140,"title":"","content":"I could see this working out if everyone there were dragonbloods, if they don't exalt they die because of the conditions but the dragonbloods are resilient enough to survive the conditions. Seems a bit morbid but the &quot;normies&quot; would need to not make it to the point they could exalt with other shards, that or have some kind of explanation as to what is keeping sidereal, lunar, and solar tier shards away","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T13:08:34-07:00","id":1403146,"title":"","content":"The rarity of such shards is explanation enough in my view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T10:17:24-07:00","id":1403246,"title":"","content":"Well, my main question is - what about the neighbors? What kind of critters, mundane or supernatural, would those people have or not to deal with and how might them help or hinder their escape or continued survival through the eras.<br /> <br /> - Pelagic beasts, beastmen or mostly forgotten primordial races?<br /> - Elementals, formed by the back &amp; forth of underwater essence currents or the actions of sorcerers human or inhuman?<br /> - Gods, demons or ghosts of all sorts and tempers out to help, exploit or poach that community of underwater humans in who knows how many ways....<br /> - Raksha exiles or even stranger emigres from the non-places beyond the borders of Creation?<br /> <br /> As an aside, do you <b>need </b>it to be a Usurpation-tied event? I think it could work just as well with the ship being a Late Shogunate treasure (possibly made by an ambitious/enterprising/vain Dragon-Blooded daimyo or general) lost in the upheaval and devastation of Contagion and Balorian Crusade. In fact that period might even justify a healthy &quot;let's keep to ourselves a little before looking for home&quot; attitude/paranoia from the survivors in ways the Usurpation would probably not.<br /> <br /> Let's not forget, &quot;just&quot; the Contagion gives you 7+ centuries of a variety of possible interactions/history for the place. Basically from Rome's colapse in 476AD to almost the 7th Crusade (definitely the siege of Jerusalem that spurred it). That's a pretty respectable time span of history to mess or be messed with.<br /> <br /> Just my two cents of thought to add or complicate the subject a bit. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T20:10:17-07:00","id":1403327,"title":"","content":"Well, I've focussed more on the vessel itself before its surroundings. The intended use for it would be for the PCs to find it, befriend the residents, repair the controller for the ballast tanks, refloat the vessel, and things get complicated (more than they already are). After centuries of undesired neglect, the <i>Sarli</i> will need a lot of repairs to be functional again: the propulsion system, steering, navigation, the various displays, possibly communication (not that there's anyone with whom it can connect). Not including the problems of decompression sickness, and how and if to maintain the tanks' unique high-pressure ecosystem.<br /> <br /> Essentially, the vessel isn't an Artifact itself, but an imperishable hull holding many First Age Artifacts that perform the various functions a ship, especially a submersible, needs just to be a ship. That's also why it needs to be a First Age vessel: imperishable things became impossible after the Usurpation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 07-18-2020, 12:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T18:35:46-07:00","id":1403451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400897-a-profoundly-isolated-society?p=1403327#post1403327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.Essentially, the vessel isn't an Artifact itself, but an imperishable hull holding many First Age Artifacts that perform the various functions a ship, especially a submersible, needs just to be a ship. That's also why it needs to be a First Age vessel: imperishable things became impossible after the Usurpation.</div> </div> </div> </div>NOT If It is the folly/vanity project of some powerful daimyo. They are NOT the norm by any stretch of imagination, but enterprising heroes exist to make the improbable/impossible happen.<br /> <br /> In fact i would say Shogunate relic goes better with the &quot;imperishable, but far from pristine&quot; angle you're going for the adventure, but it's your game and up to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T23:40:58-07:00","id":1403490,"title":"","content":"Traditionally, the Art of Permenance is associated with Solars alone.<br /> <br /> That said... things like the Sceptre of Power, Realm Defence Grid, Eye of Autochothon, Penitent etc. where all built by Solars and outlasted their creators. There's no reason why the ship couldn't have been <i>built</i> pre-Usurpation but lost during the Great Contagion. Hundreds of years in the hands of Dragon-Blooded making crude patch jobs might explain why it sank in the first place.<br /> <br /> It seems a little incongruous to say &quot;the hull is imperishable but the other systems aren't&quot;. Well why not?<br /> <br /> What if it was conceived as a pleasure barge, pushed into combat service by a Shogunate that couldn't adequately repair damage to systems never intended for combat. Last mission designed to evacuate a functional colony to escape the Great Contagion (few Deebs because they'd already been infected, explaining why the Captain didn't have the skills to rescue them and why the first generation or two might choose to just stay underwater).<br /> <br /> I mean, it absolutely works as a shop lost during the Usurpation. If that's your vision, then cool. But there's no reason to think that an imperishable ship couldn't have survived the fall of the Solars only to be lost later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T06:50:59-07:00","id":1403521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400897-a-profoundly-isolated-society?p=1403490#post1403490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Traditionally, the Art of Permenance is associated with Solars alone.<br /> <br /> That said... things like the Sceptre of Power, Realm Defence Grid, Eye of Autochothon, Penitent etc. where all built by Solars and outlasted their creators. There's no reason why the ship couldn't have been <i>built</i> pre-Usurpation but lost during the Great Contagion. Hundreds of years in the hands of Dragon-Blooded making crude patch jobs might explain why it sank in the first place.<br /> <br /> It seems a little incongruous to say &quot;the hull is imperishable but the other systems aren't&quot;. Well why not?<br /> <br /> What if it was conceived as a pleasure barge, pushed into combat service by a Shogunate that couldn't adequately repair damage to systems never intended for combat. Last mission designed to evacuate a functional colony to escape the Great Contagion (few Deebs because they'd already been infected, explaining why the Captain didn't have the skills to rescue them and why the first generation or two might choose to just stay underwater).<br /> <br /> I mean, it absolutely works as a shop lost during the Usurpation. If that's your vision, then cool. But there's no reason to think that an imperishable ship couldn't have survived the fall of the Solars only to be lost later.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because anything imperishable must be built directly and personally by a Solar, only some components were so built; much was contracted out. Those require maintenance, and so now need to be repaired or replaced. The hit that wrecked the ballast tank hatch controller was an incredible fluke in both effect and timing. And yes, only one controller was very bad design, butt as I see it, the <i>Sarli</i> was an experimental vessel, the first submersible not meant for the exclusive use of Water Aspects, so... You're right that it could gone down at any time, I just like the idea of it being lost on its first long voyage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T07:54:55-07:00","id":1403525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400897-a-profoundly-isolated-society?p=1403327#post1403327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I've focused more on the vessel itself before its surroundings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Way i see the matter, it's not so much about surroundings as the fact a crew/survivors won't exist in a vacuum unless you make it so. Desperate people pray, ergo SOMETHING, be It a god, demon, elemental, ghost or whatever (or all of those) may listen and listening, choose to answer, court, exploit, ignore, prey or any of a number of actions and depending on the critters' capacities or tempers, lead to all kind of interactions, reactions, consequences and changes.<br /> <br /> You don't have to think anything too complex - go to the Antagonists section, look at any one QC, mortal or not, and think &quot;could It or some variant exist in the sunken ship-town or lurk in its vicinity (specially relevant with immaterial beings)? And how might It affect the place, for good and for ill?&quot;<br /> <br /> It's also one of the reasons i suggested a Contagion instead of Usurpation era ship. The more time, the more crazy room for weird stuff to happen and evolve.<br /> <br /> OR alternatively, you could have the place full of ghost tripulants still lost in the obsessive (but now unnecessary) mechanical maintenance of their past tasks through the centuries, if you want to stick things to a kind of minimalism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-19-2020, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}